# The caller of a constructor function allocates without reading the prototype where the run time knows the one function object: the definition runs once, nothing replaces the prototype property or one operation assigns it before every read, and the function captures nothing, so that the closure table can create the closure. With another new.target the construction stays generic: new.target selects what is allocated, and the prototype object of a function names no layout
